# TudorVictors is Chequered Ink's, **© 2020 All Rights Reserved by the file's own `name` table**.
# No licence was bought, and the licences on offer grant use of the face to make things rather than
# the right to redistribute the file. Withdrawn from the bundle at export 11; §9's wordmark ships as
# artwork instead (`design/assets/gatecrasher-wordmark.png`). Nothing should ever put it back.
#
# **This rule matched ONE LITERAL PATH and that is how the file came to be committed.** It pinned
# `design/assets/TudorVictors.ttf`; the bundle delivered to `design/fonts/`, one directory over, so
# the rule did not fire and `88b862f` committed a font we have no right to redistribute. That is
# the SECOND time this exact mechanism has bitten this casting — the first was an `old/` of 44
# files carrying a second copy of the same font, for the same reason, recorded in the root
# CLAUDE.md. A rule that names a path only protects that path.
#
# So it matches the NAME, anywhere. The two stale halves of the note this replaces are worth
# knowing about: it said the font "arrives in each design bundle", which stopped being true at
# export 11, and that "as of Rev 6 the wordmark is baked into gatecrasher-panel-plate@2x.png, so
# nothing in the build needs it" — the plate was deleted in the panel rewrite and the build DID
# need it, which is what made the committed copy load-bearing rather than merely present.
TudorVictors.ttf
**/TudorVictors.ttf

# Designer hand-off archives land in handoff/, which is ignored whole. design/ holds only the
# design the plugin is CURRENTLY built from, so the two never have to be told apart by timestamp:
# handoff/ is what arrived, design/ is what is in use, and the merge from one to the other is the
# deliberate step between them.
#
# design/*.zip stays as a guard, not because archives go there any more. Dropping one in design/ was
# the habit for a long time, and an untracked stray is cheaper than a 15MB binary committed by
# reflex.
#
# design/assets/ must stay TRACKED: the plate, knob strips, icons and the two runtime fonts are
# build inputs, so an untracked design/ is a repo that does not build.
design/*.zip
handoff/

# Prompt logs are personal working notes, not project documentation. Any decision that matters
# belongs in a code comment beside what it governs, or in this repo's CLAUDE.md - never only in a
# prompt, where nobody will find it.
prompts/
